## OpenAI Codex — carried forward from `NOTICE`

- Upstream: OpenAI Codex, <https://github.com/openai/codex>
- Commit: `67f0994b532b8740f14b5b738af7b7b2a915b1d6`
- Licence: Apache-2.0
- Source of this notice: `NOTICE` at the repository root of that commit

Carried forward (its first line and copyright; the Ratatui paragraph covers
Codex's terminal UI, which MatOpt does not use):

> OpenAI Codex
> Copyright 2025 OpenAI

No Codex file is vendored. These MatOpt modules are Python reimplementations
of mechanics in `codex-rs/`, written against MatOpt's own harness and adapted
to it; each names the crate or file it follows (see
[`docs/CODEX-INTEGRATION.md`](docs/CODEX-INTEGRATION.md)):
`backend/app/agent/exec_output.py`, `exec_rules.py`, `sandbox.py`, `hooks.py`,
`instructions.py`, `turn_diff.py`, `text_match.py`, `tools/exec_sessions.py`,
`backend/app/llm/retry.py`, and the Codex-derived parts of `harness.py`,
`compaction.py` and `mcp/client.py`. The Seatbelt profile in `sandbox.py` is
MatOpt's own; it reuses Codex's fixed `system-fcntl` deny.

